"],["ARC or PLC in Stafford County","/arc-plc/kansas/stafford-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 11 grids in Stafford County runs from 1951 to 2025, and February to March and November to December each came in under 90% of normal in 40 of those 75 years. In 2025, August to September ran 164% of normal on the middle of the grids, while February to March sat at 19% in 2025. So far in 2026, March to April came in at 11% of normal on the middle of the grids. Every grid had its driest year in 1956.</p>"}
